{card:Index}
{widgets}
title:{"type":"field","size":[492,17],"pos":[10,22],"locked":1,"font":"menu","show":"invert","border":1,"align":"center","value":"Rich Text Exercises"}
blurb:{"type":"field","size":[492,92],"pos":[10,48],"locked":1,"border":0,"value":"Exercises for the RText interface and for fonts in fields. Each card gives you a function to write and a Check button that runs it against a sample field. They are meant to be solved with the Decker documentation (RText Interface, Field Interface, Canvas Interface) open beside you; there are no solutions in this deck.\n\nThe sample field on cards 1-4 must not be edited, since the checkers look for specific words in it."}
list:{"type":"field","size":[492,110],"pos":[10,150],"locked":1,"script":"Index.1","border":0,"value":{"text":["1. Which font is it?","\n","2. Where do the runs begin and end?","\n","3. Which run holds this match? (a trap)","\n","4. Find the hyperlinks","\n","5. Where is it on screen?","\n"],"font":["menu","","menu","","menu","","menu","","menu",""],"arg":["ex1","","ex2","","ex3","","ex4","","ex5",""]}}

{script:Index.1}
on link val do
 go[val "BoxIn" 15]
end
{end}

{card:ex1}
{widgets}
title:{"type":"field","size":[492,17],"pos":[10,22],"locked":1,"font":"menu","show":"invert","border":1,"align":"center","value":"1. Which font is it?"}
prompt:{"type":"field","size":[492,76],"pos":[10,44],"locked":1,"border":0,"value":"A field has a default font (field.font), and each run in its rich text may override it in the font column. Write fontAt[f p]: given a field f and a character position p, return the name of the font that character is drawn in. Look at rtext.get[], and remember that an empty font cell means \"inherit\". Open question once it passes: what does an invalid font name do? Settle it by experiment, not by guessing."}
sample:{"type":"field","size":[492,34],"pos":[10,124],"locked":1,"value":{"text":["Plain text, ","mono bit"," back to plain, ","menu bit"," then a ","link"," and ","another","."],"font":["","mono","","menu","","","","",""],"arg":["","","","","","somewhere","","elsewhere",""]}}
code:{"type":"field","size":[300,128],"pos":[10,164],"style":"code","scrollbar":1,"value":"# Return the name of the font actually used to draw\n# character position p of field f.\n# Remember: an empty font cell means \"use f.font\".\non fontAt f p do\n \"?\"\nend"}
check:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[320,164],"script":"ex1.1","text":"Check","style":"rect"}
out:{"type":"field","size":[182,118],"pos":[320,188],"locked":1,"volatile":1,"border":1,"scrollbar":1,"value":""}
prev:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[10,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Prev","style":"rect"}
index:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[78,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Index","style":"rect"}
next:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[442,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Next","style":"rect"}

{script:ex1.0}
on click do
 t.Prev:"SlideRight"
 t.Next:"SlideLeft"
 t.Index:"BoxOut"
 go[me.text t[me.text] 15]
end
{end}

{script:ex1.1}
on click do
 r:eval[code.text () 1]
 if r.error
  out.text:"Your code did not run:\n%s" format r.error
 else
  fontAt:r.vars.fontAt
  words:"Plain","mono","back","menu"
  want :"body","mono","body","menu"
  got:each w in words fontAt[sample 2+first first rtext.find[sample.value w]] end
  out.text:"%i of 4 correct.\n\ngot:  %s\nwant: %s" format (sum got=want),("%j" format list got),("%j" format list want)
 end
end
{end}

{card:ex2}
{widgets}
title:{"type":"field","size":[492,17],"pos":[10,22],"locked":1,"font":"menu","show":"invert","border":1,"align":"center","value":"2. Where do the runs begin and end?"}
prompt:{"type":"field","size":[492,76],"pos":[10,44],"locked":1,"border":0,"value":"Runs are rows, but all of Decker's rtext functions speak in character positions. Write runBounds[t]: given an rtext table, return a list of (start,end) position pairs, one per run, so that rtext.span[t (start,end)] gives you back exactly that run. Row text lengths are all you need. Think about what rtext.cat[] would do to two neighbouring rows with identical styling, and why you should always cast with rtext.cat[] first."}
sample:{"type":"field","size":[492,34],"pos":[10,124],"locked":1,"value":{"text":["Plain text, ","mono bit"," back to plain, ","menu bit"," then a ","link"," and ","another","."],"font":["","mono","","menu","","","","",""],"arg":["","","","","","somewhere","","elsewhere",""]}}
code:{"type":"field","size":[300,128],"pos":[10,164],"style":"code","scrollbar":1,"value":"# Given an rtext table t, return a list of (start,end)\n# character-position pairs, one per run (row).\non runBounds t do\n ()\nend"}
check:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[320,164],"script":"ex2.1","text":"Check","style":"rect"}
out:{"type":"field","size":[182,118],"pos":[320,188],"locked":1,"volatile":1,"border":1,"scrollbar":1,"value":""}
prev:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[10,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Prev","style":"rect"}
index:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[78,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Index","style":"rect"}
next:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[442,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Next","style":"rect"}

{script:ex2.1}
on click do
 r:eval[code.text () 1]
 if r.error
  out.text:"Your code did not run:\n%s" format r.error
 else
  runBounds:r.vars.runBounds
  want:(list 0,12),(list 12,20),(list 20,36),(list 36,44),(list 44,52),(list 52,56),(list 56,61),(list 61,68),(list 68,69)
  got:runBounds[rtext.cat[sample.value]]
  if got~want
   out.text:"Correct!"
  else
   out.text:"Not yet.\n\ngot:\n%s\n\nwant:\n%s" format ("%j" format list got),("%j" format list want)
  end
 end
end
{end}

{card:ex3}
{widgets}
title:{"type":"field","size":[492,17],"pos":[10,22],"locked":1,"font":"menu","show":"invert","border":1,"align":"center","value":"3. Which run holds this match?"}
prompt:{"type":"field","size":[492,76],"pos":[10,44],"locked":1,"border":0,"value":"Write runOf[t w]: return the row number of the run containing the FIRST CHARACTER of the first case-insensitive match of w in t. The obvious answer, rtext.get[t start-of-match], gets some of the six test words wrong. Run it and see which, then work out why. (Positions are the gaps between characters, not the characters themselves. Which run does a boundary gap belong to?)"}
sample:{"type":"field","size":[492,34],"pos":[10,124],"locked":1,"value":{"text":["Plain text, ","mono bit"," back to plain, ","menu bit"," then a ","link"," and ","another","."],"font":["","mono","","menu","","","","",""],"arg":["","","","","","somewhere","","elsewhere",""]}}
code:{"type":"field","size":[300,128],"pos":[10,164],"style":"code","scrollbar":1,"value":"# Return the row number of the run containing the\n# first *character* of the first (case-insensitive)\n# match of the string w in rtext table t.\n# Hint: compare what rtext.find and rtext.get say\n# at a run boundary. Positions are gaps BETWEEN chars.\non runOf t w do\n -1\nend"}
check:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[320,164],"script":"ex3.1","text":"Check","style":"rect"}
out:{"type":"field","size":[182,118],"pos":[320,188],"locked":1,"volatile":1,"border":1,"scrollbar":1,"value":""}
prev:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[10,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Prev","style":"rect"}
index:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[78,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Index","style":"rect"}
next:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[442,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Next","style":"rect"}

{script:ex3.1}
on click do
 r:eval[code.text () 1]
 if r.error
  out.text:"Your code did not run:\n%s" format r.error
 else
  runOf:r.vars.runOf
  words:"Plain","mono","back","menu","then","link"
  want :0,1,2,3,4,5
  got:each w in words runOf[rtext.cat[sample.value] w] end
  out.text:"%i of 6 correct.\n\ngot:  %s\nwant: %s" format (sum got=want),("%j" format list got),("%j" format list want)
 end
end
{end}

{card:ex4}
{widgets}
title:{"type":"field","size":[492,17],"pos":[10,22],"locked":1,"font":"menu","show":"invert","border":1,"align":"center","value":"4. Find the hyperlinks"}
prompt:{"type":"field","size":[492,76],"pos":[10,44],"locked":1,"border":0,"value":"Write links[t]: return the text of every run of t that is a hyperlink, in order. A run is a hyperlink if its arg is a non-empty string. (An arg that is an image makes it an inline image instead. The sample has none, but your code could be made to cope.) Try a query on the table rather than a loop, if you are feeling brave."}
sample:{"type":"field","size":[492,34],"pos":[10,124],"locked":1,"value":{"text":["Plain text, ","mono bit"," back to plain, ","menu bit"," then a ","link"," and ","another","."],"font":["","mono","","menu","","","","",""],"arg":["","","","","","somewhere","","elsewhere",""]}}
code:{"type":"field","size":[300,128],"pos":[10,164],"style":"code","scrollbar":1,"value":"# Return a list of the text of every run of rtext\n# table t that is a hyperlink (non-empty string arg).\non links t do\n ()\nend"}
check:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[320,164],"script":"ex4.1","text":"Check","style":"rect"}
out:{"type":"field","size":[182,118],"pos":[320,188],"locked":1,"volatile":1,"border":1,"scrollbar":1,"value":""}
prev:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[10,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Prev","style":"rect"}
index:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[78,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Index","style":"rect"}
next:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[442,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Next","style":"rect"}

{script:ex4.1}
on click do
 r:eval[code.text () 1]
 if r.error
  out.text:"Your code did not run:\n%s" format r.error
 else
  links:r.vars.links
  want:"link","another"
  got:links[rtext.cat[sample.value]]
  if got~want
   out.text:"Correct!"
  else
   out.text:"Not yet.\n\ngot:  %s\nwant: %s" format ("%j" format list got),("%j" format list want)
  end
 end
end
{end}

{card:ex5}
{widgets}
title:{"type":"field","size":[492,17],"pos":[10,22],"locked":1,"font":"menu","show":"invert","border":1,"align":"center","value":"5. Where is it on screen?"}
prompt:{"type":"field","size":[492,76],"pos":[10,44],"locked":1,"border":0,"value":"Write pixelPos[f p]: return the (x,y) pixel position, relative to the top-left corner of field f, where character position p begins. Press Mark to draw red boxes at your answers for several positions in the paragraph below. Decker offers no direct way to ask this, so you will have to measure text yourself with canvas.textsize[], remembering that word-wrapping the whole text is not the same as word-wrapping a prefix of it. What padding does a field apply? Find out. Stretch goal: go the other way and turn pointer.pos into a character position."}
para:{"type":"field","size":[300,112],"pos":[10,124],"locked":1,"border":1,"value":{"text":["Decker lays out rich text itself, so there is no function that converts a character position to a pixel position. You have to rebuild the answer from the pieces the docs do give you: field.offset, field.size, field.scroll, canvas.textsize[] and its optional wrap width, and the fonts of the runs. The needle is hiding right ","here",", in the middle of a wrapped paragraph, with a ","second"," one near the end for good measure. needle."],"font":["","mono","","menu",""],"arg":["","","","",""]}}
mark:{"type":"canvas","size":[300,112],"pos":[10,124],"show":"transparent","locked":1}
code:{"type":"field","size":[182,184],"pos":[320,124],"style":"code","scrollbar":1,"value":"# return (x,y) of char position p in field f\non pixelPos f p do\n (0,0)\nend"}
check:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[10,240],"script":"ex5.1","text":"Mark","style":"rect"}
out:{"type":"field","size":[232,60],"pos":[78,240],"locked":1,"volatile":1,"border":1,"value":""}
prev:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[10,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Prev","style":"rect"}
index:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[78,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Index","style":"rect"}
next:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[442,312],"script":"ex1.0","text":"Next","style":"rect"}

{script:ex5.1}
on click do
 r:eval[code.text () 1]
 mark.clear[]
 mark.pattern:colors.red
 if r.error
  out.text:"Your code did not run:\n%s" format r.error
 else
  pixelPos:r.vars.pixelPos
  ps:(0,rtext.len[para.value]),(each m in rtext.find[para.value "needle" 1] first m end)
  each p in ps
   xy:pixelPos[para p]
   mark.box[(xy-2) (5,5)]
  end
  out.text:"Marked %i positions:\n%s" format (count ps),("%j" format list ps)
 end
end
{end}
